  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity building of paprika smallholder farmers in Mwenezi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zimbabwe&#x2019;s economy is primarily reliant upon agriculture, which employs 60%-70% of the population and generates 40% of all export revenue. Due to this dependency, when local agriculture struggles, the rest of the economy suffers too. Supporting the smallholder farmers is one of the Netherlands&#x2019; priority areas for development cooperation in Zimbabwe. Zimbabwe has successfully exploited markets for high-value non-traditional agricultural products, most notably horticultural crops, in industrialised countries.This paprika value-chain project will provide training and technical extension support to at least 1,000 smallholder farmers on paprika nursery establishment and management, field production and post-harvest management. The project will also scale up the production of other spices such as coriander, fennel and fenugreek, which have a ready and guaranteed offtake market to Europe.</narrative>
  </description>
